# project: oncall-overhaul
VAR shadow_cycles = 0

-> alert_audit

=== alert_audit ===
Audit every alert; delete or tune the noisy ones.
Done looks like a full pass over the alert inventory with deletions and tuning applied, aiming for under ten pages per week.
+ [Not livable yet — keep tuning] @human ~loop~ -> alert_audit
+ [Under ten pages a week and actually livable] @human -> rotation_design

=== rotation_design ===
Design the new on-call rotation to run alongside the old one.
Done looks like a rota schedule ready to enter its first shadow cycle.
* [Design ready — start shadowing] -> shadow_cycle

=== shadow_cycle ===
Run the new rota alongside the old one for a full cycle, with new folks shadowing every page.
~ shadow_cycles += 1
+ [Cycle complete — capture what shadowing found] -> runbook_gap_writeup

=== runbook_gap_writeup ===
Write up every runbook gap found during shadowing; gaps must be documented before the next cycle starts.
+ {shadow_cycles < 2} [Gaps written up — run the next shadow cycle] ~loop~ -> shadow_cycle
+ {shadow_cycles >= 2} [Shadowing complete — request sign-off] -> primary_signoff

=== primary_signoff ===
The SRE lead reviews the shadow cycles and decides whether the new rotation goes primary.
+ [Signed off — new rota goes primary] @human -> first_month_primary
+ [Not ready — run another shadow cycle] @human ~loop~ -> shadow_cycle

=== first_month_primary ===
The new rotation is primary for its first month, with the old rota kept on standby.
Watch incidents for anything that exposes a flaw in the rotation design itself.
+ [Stable month — retire the old rota] @human -> retire_old_rota
+ [Incident exposed a rotation design flaw — revert to old rota] @human -> revert_and_fix

=== revert_and_fix ===
The old rota is primary again while the rotation design flaw is fixed.
Done looks like a corrected design ready to re-prove itself in one more shadow cycle.
+ [Design fixed — re-run one shadow cycle] ~loop~ -> shadow_cycle

=== retire_old_rota ===
The old rota is switched off and archived; the new rotation is the only rotation.
* [Old rota retired] -> blameless_review

=== blameless_review ===
Blameless review of the whole overhaul: alert tuning, shadowing, the cutover, and any revert, with lessons written down.
-> END
